<title>SLOVAKIA: Slovakia posts Jan-Nov 96 c/a deficit of $1.4 bln.</title>
<headline>Slovakia posts Jan-Nov 96 c/a deficit of $1.4 bln.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Slovak current account</p>
<p>recorded a deficit for the January-November period of $1.4</p>
<p>billion, compared with a $480.6 million surplus for the same</p>
<p>period in 1995, the central bank said on Monday.</p>
<p>It added that the capital account was in surplus for the</p>
<p>first 11 months of 1996 by $1.57 billion, compared with a</p>
<p>surplus of $332.3 million for the same period of the previous</p>
<p>year.</p>
<p> SLOVAK CURRENT ACCT    11MO'96    10MO'96    FY/95   11MO'95</p>
<p>  overall ($ million)  -1,400.5   -1,174.1   +648.8    +480.6</p>
<p>  trade balance	  -1,596.8   -1,392.6    +24.1    -122.0</p>
<p>  balance of services     +37.9	+80.5   +546.2    +530.9</p>
<p>  income balance	    -22.6	-16.0    -13.7	-3.5</p>
<p>  current transfers	+181.0     +154.0    +92.2     +75.1</p>
<p> CAPITAL ACCOUNT</p>
<p>  Total balance	    -1,571.6  -1,252.4  +993.9  +332.3</p>
<p>  capital transfers	   +29.7     +29.8   +45.7   +45.7</p>
<p>direct investment balance</p>
<p>   inv. in Slovak Republic +108.8    +108.3  +141.9  +105.2</p>
<p>   Slovak investment abroad -45.1     -33.2    -7.9    -8.3</p>
<p>portfolio investment balance</p>
<p>   inv. in Slovak Republic   +5.7	+5.7   +74.4    +4.8</p>
<p>   Slovak investment abroad +61.7     +68.3  +171.7  +184.6</p>
<p>other long-term financial</p>
<p>   account		     +496.3    +349.5  +393.8   +69.6</p>
<p>  short-term fin. account  +914.5    +724.1   +91.3   -26.3</p>
<p>Note. All figures are in millions of U.S. dollars. The</p>
<p>central bank used the following exchange rates in calculating</p>
<p>the figures: Jan-Nov '96 (USD=30.571 SKK), Jan-Oct'96</p>
<p>(USD=30.536 SKK), full year '95 (USD=29.735 SKK), Jan-Nov '95</p>
<p>(USD=29.737).</p>
<p>-- Bratislava Newsroom, 42-7-5218-402</p>
</text>
